# Accurate Codebase Analysis

RULE: When analyzing codebase architecture or counting patterns, exclude `.venv*/**`, `node_modules/**`, `build/**`, `tests/**`, and `*.md` from searches. Use ripgrep with `--glob '!.venv*'` (and equivalent). Check for evolved patterns (e.g. `setup_service` vs `setup_events`) before reporting violations.
WHY: Searching without exclusions counts installed packages and tests as "your code" — e.g. 5,697 "GCS imports" when production code has 0.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/accurate-codebase-analysis.md

DO:
  rg "pattern" --type py --glob '!.venv*/**' --glob '!tests/**' --glob '!*_test.py' --glob '!test_*.py'
  Exclude .venv, tests, docs, scripts when counting production violations
  Check for newer equivalent patterns before claiming something is missing
  Treat abstraction layers (e.g. unified-cloud-interface/providers/gcp.py) and conftest.py as legitimate exceptions

NEVER:
  rg "pattern"  # no globs — includes .venv and installed packages
  Count .venv or site-packages as "code with issues"
  Conflate test-only patterns with production architectural violations
  Report violations without verifying scope (excluded paths, command used)

See CODEX for full exclusion list, verification checklist, reporting template, and special cases.
